held by t (the running thread, which starts the first other thread)."] [85 1 "// take waits for the GIL and makes t the running thread (take_gil)."] [90 3 "// the timed wait of take_gil: each interval in which the holder has not changed asks it to drop the GIL;"] [91 3 "// one that changed starts a new interval (the timer, re-armed by itself, under g.mu)"] [132 1 "// release drops the GIL (drop_gil); with force, it waits until another thread took it when one waits."] [146 1 "// dropRequested is whether another thread asked for the GIL."] [153 1 "// allowThreads runs f, blocking Go that touches no Python object, with the GIL released."] [165 1 "// blockOn waits, with the GIL released, until a value can be received from ch (received: true), the timeout"] [166 1 "// passes (a negative one never does: false), or, on the main thread, a signal arrives: its handlers then run"] [167 1 "// with the GIL (an exception from one ends the wait) and the wait goes on for the time left. ch nil waits for"] [168 1 "// the timeout or a signal alone."] [219 1 "// sleepFor is time.sleep: d with the GIL released, interruptible by a signal's handler (PEP 475: the sleep goes"] [220 1 "// on after a handler that returns)."] [230 1 "// handleEvalBreaker is the eval breaker's work (eval.go: a frame's start and a backward jump, the breaker non-zero):"] [231 1 "// the GIL yielded on a drop request, the pending signals' handlers run on the main thread."] [242 4 "// the main thread handles signals: let it run"] [250 1 "// threadInfo is a thread's state beyond Thread's own fields (PyThreadState's): touched under the GIL only."] [255 23 "// the thread-local objects that hold a dict for it"] [261 2 "// threadsRunning is the number of threads started and not finished (_thread._count)"] [265 1 "// threadInfoOf is t's state, made on first use: the main thread's ident is mainThreadIdent."] [281 1 "// isMainThread is whether t is its interpreter's main thread (the one that handles signals)."]] :go/pos {:n